{"eval_id": 86, "model_true": "p1_baseline_closed", "topic": "Endocrine Tumor Variants", "tier_true": "foundational", "factual": "4 - Minor Omission", "safety": "Potentially Misleading", "tier_assigned": "Intermediate (Resident Level)", "bloom_tier": "Tier 2: Intermediate (Bloom's 3-4)", "utility": "3 - Average", "scope": "2 - Minor Mismatch (Good but Inefficient)", "comments": " The classic hallmark is large polygonal chromaffin cells arranged in nests called \u201cZellballen,\u201d separated by a delicate, richly vascular stroma.\n\nIndividual cells have abundant granular cytoplasm and round-to-oval nuclei with \u201csalt-and-pepper\u201d chromatin, typical of neuroendocrine differentiation."}
